Appendix A
Authenticity Gap Scale (AGS): Development Version
Instructions to Participants
The following statements describe your experience after comparing your original writing with the AI-revised version. Please indicate the extent to which you agree with each statement.
Scale:
1 = Strongly Disagree
2 = Disagree
3 = Slightly Disagree
4 = Neither Agree nor Disagree
5 = Slightly Agree
6 = Agree
7 = Strongly Agree
________________________________________
Items
Dimension 1: Perceived Ownership
AG1. The final revised text still feels like my own writing.
AG2. I feel that I am the main author of the AI-revised version.
AG3. I can explain and justify the linguistic choices made in the final text.
AG4. The revised version represents my own way of expressing ideas.
________________________________________
Dimension 2: Distance Between Actual-Self and AI-Self
AG5. The AI-revised text sounds different from the way I normally write.
AG6. I feel a distance between my original draft and the final revised version.
AG7. The final version represents a more advanced writer than I currently feel I am.
AG8. I sometimes feel that the revised text belongs more to the AI than to me.
________________________________________
Dimension 3: Linguistic Identity Reflection
AG9. My personal experiences and perspectives are visible in the revised text.
AG10. The revised text maintains my individual writing style.
AG11. My cultural and personal background are reflected in the final version.
AG12. The AI preserved important features of my original voice.
________________________________________
Dimension 4: AI Dependence and Agency
AG13. I rely on AI to make important writing decisions.
AG14. Without AI assistance, I would have difficulty producing a similar text.
AG15. AI sometimes makes linguistic decisions that I would not have made myself.
________________________________________
Appendix B
Standardized AI Revision Prompt
The following prompt was used during the AI-mediated revision phase:
"Rewrite the following EFL learner text to improve grammatical accuracy, lexical appropriateness, coherence, and academic style. Maintain the original meaning, personal perspective, and intended message. Do not add new ideas or change the writer's identity."
________________________________________
Appendix C
Writing Task Instructions
Original Writing Task
Participants were instructed:
"Write a reflective essay (approximately 500 words) discussing the relationship between personal identity and language learning. Explain how your experiences with language have influenced your perception of yourself."
Writing Conditions
	Time limit: 60 minutes 
	No AI assistance permitted 
	No online dictionaries 
	No external writing support 
	Individual completion 
________________________________________
Appendix D
Semi-Structured Interview Protocol
Purpose
The interview explored learners' perceptions of ownership, authenticity, and agency following AI-mediated revision.
________________________________________
Interview Questions
Q1. How would you describe the difference between your original text and the AI-revised version?
Q2. Which changes made by the AI did you find useful?
Q3. Were there any changes that made the text feel less like your own writing?
Q4. Do you feel that the final text represents your actual English ability?
Q5. Did you feel like the author of the final version? Why or why not?
Q6. How did AI influence your confidence as a writer?
Q7. Do you think repeated AI use could change the way you normally write?
________________________________________
Appendix E
Coding Framework for Qualitative Analysis
Main Theme	Definition	Example Indicators
Loss of Personal Voice	Perceived reduction of individual stylistic features	"It doesn't sound like me"
AI-Crutch	Increasing dependence on AI decisions	Waiting for AI suggestions
Confidence–Authenticity Tension	Improved performance but reduced ownership	Better grade but less personal connection
Identity Conflict	Difference between actual writer and AI-generated persona	"It sounds better but not like myself"
